  "body": "Separated into three fairly-distinct commits. Still work to do, but this can stand on its own for now.\n\nThe third commit could benefit from some additional prose around the new \"current settings object\" concept. https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27204 and https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26603 and https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27203 all touch on that a bit. Ideally we would expand the `a.html`/`b.html` example to show a case where the current settings object is different from the other two, and expand the non-normative note to say what the current settings object is used for or should be used for.\n\nBut, maybe that can wait until I actually dive into those three bugs, by auditing all existing incumbent and entry settings object usages, and seeing if @bholley says it's OK to replace them with current settings object.\n\nA review from @bzbarsky would be helpful, at least for the second commit. The first commit is fairly easy and I am fairly confident in it; the third commit is mostly editorial and consists of updating a lot of cross-references to reference newly-introduced correspondences between the three 1:1:1 things.\n",
